    "body": "Docs only. Applies the deferred design-doc updates from the operating-hours PRs to SPEC-0012 `spec.md` and `design.md`, so the docs describe what shipped. Also moves SPEC-0012 from `draft` to `implemented` and ADR-0019 from `proposed` to `accepted`.\n\n## What each source contributed\n\n| Source | Update | Where |\n|---|---|---|\n| #389 \"Deferred Design Doc Updates\" | Autostart begins every enabled gated harness held unless a lease covers it, and the first gate evaluation (which runs at scheduler start) releases the in-hours ones. New scenario \"Boot in hours\". | spec REQ \"Gate Enforcement\"; design \u00a7 \"`Hold` and `Release` on the Manager\" |\n| #389 \"Deferred Design Doc Updates\" | Reload (ADR-0014) and `use-profile` record intent and begin a down gated harness held (`startOrHold` / `EnableHeld`). | same |\n| #389 body | A hold does **not** reuse `gracefulStopKeepEnabled`, which could persist `enabled=false`. `gracefulStop` consumes the exit itself. | design \u00a7 \"`Hold` and `Release`\" |\n| #396 (no deferred section; reconciled against the code) | `StartFor` and the op's routing (explicit `for`, default `DefaultLease` via `LeaseApplies`, `ErrNoLease`). What a crash between write and start actually leaves: boot starts only an `enabled` harness, otherwise the lease expires. `Restore` drops a lease that lost its hours. The lease's end anchors the close. | spec REQ \"After-Hours Lease\"; design \u00a7 \"Leases in `state.json`\" |\n| #401/#403 (no deferred section; the original #401 body was recovered from its edit history) | The gate pass pseudo-code as built (`Status`/`Lease`/`CloseAt`/`Hold`/`CloseStep`/`Arm`, arm lead, per-decision goroutines). `Expr.PrevEnd`. The `TurnBridge` seam, first sample, poll and linger backstop. Zero in-window events read as quiet (the #401 review's note 3). Open questions record what shipped. | design \u00a7\u00a7 \"A pure `internal/hours` package\", \"Evaluate on the existing scheduler tick\", \"Turn state from a daemon-side watcher\", \"Open Questions\"; spec REQ \"Graceful Shutdown\" |\n| This review's fixes | The lease is judged on the tick's clock, a lease ends at its end instant and is discarded when hours open (#409), the close is stepped on the tick that began it (#409), and a restart cancels a close (#410). | spec REQ \"After-Hours Lease\", REQ \"Graceful Shutdown\"; design gate pass |\n\nREQ \"Operating Hours Visibility\" is untouched, because #385 is in flight. The ADR body is untouched; only its status changed.\n\n## Status vocabulary\nThe SDD plugin's statuses are `proposed / accepted / deprecated / superseded` for ADRs and `draft / review / approved / implemented / deprecated` for specs. ADR-0013 and ADR-0020 already use `accepted`. **Merge order:** `implemented` is accurate only once #385 (visibility) lands, and the lease and close lines above describe #409 and #410. Please merge this after those three.\n\n## Verification\n- Every changed sentence was checked against the code on main (and on the #409/#410 branches for the lines that describe them). File references: `internal/supervisor/manager.go` (`Autostart`, `startOrHold`, `StartFor`, `LeaseApplies`, `Restore`), `internal/supervisor/hours.go` (`hold`, `EnableHeld`), `internal/scheduler/gate.go` (`gatePass`, `dispatchGate`), `internal/runtrace/watch.go`, `internal/hours/hours.go` (`PrevEnd`), `internal/daemon/control.go` (`opLifecycle`).\n- `make check` clean.\n\nAlso covers #419's deferred update: design.md \u00a7 \"Presentation reuses the schedule machinery\" now says the zone prefix is trimmed client-side by comparing with `TZ`, and that nothing is trimmed when `TZ` is unset (commit `4590c07`). The spec's Visibility REQ doesn't mention trimming, so it is unchanged.\n\nPart of #376 \u00b7 Spec: SPEC-0012\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Posted on behalf of `@joestump` by [`claude-opus-5`](https://openrouter.ai/anthropic/claude-opus-5) using [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code).\n",
